<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Medellín Cartel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1970s–1993</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medellin">Medellín</a> Cartel was a Colombian drug-trafficking network based in Medellín that dominated the cocaine trade to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the 1980s. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-escobar">Pablo Escobar</a> with partners such as the Ochoa brothers and Carlos Lehder, it waged a campaign of bombings and assassinations against the Colombian state to prevent extradition. It collapsed after Escobar was killed in 1993.</p></div>
